WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:13.895
Orange danced near the wolves.

2
00:00:14.555 --> 00:00:16.156
They backed away in terror.

3
00:00:16.176 --> 00:00:18.918
"I'm leaving the jungle!"

4
00:00:19.298 --> 00:00:20.119
Mowgli yelled.

5
00:00:20.139 --> 00:00:22.840
"I'm going to live in the village.

6
00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.742
The humans will be kind to me."

7
00:00:26.823 --> 00:00:28.884
He stepped toward a pile of sticks.

8
00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:32.585
"Now I must pay a debt."

9
00:00:34.407 --> 00:00:37.008
He grabbed a stick and lit it from the fire.

10
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.593
Then he marched toward Shere Khan and held the stick close to the tiger's fur.

11
00:00:45.613 --> 00:00:49.275
"Remember this, Shere Khan."

12
00:00:49.695 --> 00:00:50.656
Mowgli growled.

13
00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:57.160
"The next time I come to Council Rock, I will be carrying your hide."

14
00:00:58.432 --> 00:01:01.654
He waved the burning stick even closer to the tiger.

15
00:01:01.674 --> 00:01:04.496
"And Akela goes free.

16
00:01:04.777 --> 00:01:06.478
You will not kill him!"

17
00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:10.681
The fire burned furiously at the end of the stick.

18
00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:16.184
Mowgli waved it right and left, and the frightened tiger ran off.

19
00:01:18.106 --> 00:01:22.969
Most of the wolves ran off too, howling as sparks landed on their fur.

20
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.772
Akela and Bagheera hurried over to Mowgli.

21
00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:31.909
He was gasping in pain, and tears streamed down his face.

22
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.771
happening to me, Bagheera?"

23
00:01:39.191 --> 00:01:39.651
he said.

24
00:01:39.671 --> 00:01:43.032
"Why do I feel so strange?"

25
00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:46.753
"You are feeling deep sorrow, Little Brother.

26
00:01:47.713 --> 00:01:49.074
That is why you are crying.

27
00:01:50.034 --> 00:01:52.074
Only humans shed tears like yours."

28
00:01:53.675 --> 00:01:55.996
Mowgli sat and cried for a while.

29
00:02:01.341 --> 00:02:02.541
Finally he got up.

30
00:02:02.561 --> 00:02:06.002
"I'm going back to the cave now.

31
00:02:06.742 --> 00:02:10.964
In the morning I will say farewell to Mother and Father Wolf."

32
00:02:13.484 --> 00:02:19.666
The next day the young wolves howled miserably as Mowgli stood at the mouth of the cave.

33
00:02:19.686 --> 00:02:22.667
"You won't forget me, will you?"

34
00:02:23.107 --> 00:02:23.847
Mowgli said.

35
00:02:23.867 --> 00:02:28.181
"Never!" the one named Gray Brother promised.

36
00:02:28.201 --> 00:02:32.124
"Meet us at the bottom of the hill every once in a while.

37
00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:33.844
We can play with you there."

38
00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:38.147
"We will miss you, Mowgli," Mother said softly.

39
00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:42.429
"I will meet you soon," Mowgli promised.

40
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:47.552
Then he left the cave and went down the hillside alone.

41
00:02:50.213 --> 00:02:54.676
Mowgli walked for hours along a rough road that ran down the valley.

42
00:02:56.432 --> 00:03:00.716
At last, the road opened into a wide plain.

43
00:03:01.736 --> 00:03:04.979
The plain was dotted with big rocks and trees.

44
00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.703
Herds of cattle and buffalo grazed all over the plain.

45
00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.946
In the distance Mowgli could see a village.

46
00:03:17.309 --> 00:03:28.046
Several children were in charge of the animal When they saw Mowgli, they shouted in fear and ran

47
00:03:28.106 --> 00:03:34.251
away. Hungry, Mowgli headed toward the village.

48
00:03:37.153 --> 00:03:39.775
When he reached the gate, a man came out.

49
00:03:41.737 --> 00:03:45.980
Mowgli opened his mouth and pointed down it to show that he was hungry.

50
00:03:47.241 --> 00:03:50.564
The man stared in shock and spun around.

51
00:03:51.785 --> 00:03:54.226
He ran away, shouting for the priest.

52
00:03:56.172 --> 00:04:00.095
Soon a big, fat man dressed in white came to the gate.

53
00:04:01.416 --> 00:04:03.857
He had a colorful mark on his forehead.

54
00:04:04.718 --> 00:04:06.599
Behind him was a huge crowd.

55
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.821
They all stared and pointed at Mowgli.

56
00:04:09.841 --> 00:04:13.844
"Humans have no manners," Mowgli thought.

57
00:04:13.864 --> 00:04:16.946
"Only monkeys behave like this!"

58
00:04:17.927 --> 00:04:19.187
He frowned at the crowd.

59
00:04:19.207 --> 00:04:25.812
"There's nothing to be afraid of," the priest said to the crowd.

60
00:04:27.648 --> 00:04:28.829
He pointed to Mowgli.

61
00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:33.252
"Look at these marks on the boy's arms and legs.

62
00:04:35.493 --> 00:04:36.594
They are wolf bites.

63
00:04:37.395 --> 00:04:40.437
He has probably run away from the jungle."

64
00:04:40.457 --> 00:04:43.659
"The poor child!"

65
00:04:44.179 --> 00:04:45.320
a few women said.

66
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.303
"He is a handsome boy," a woman said.

67
00:04:50.884 --> 00:04:52.825
Suddenly one woman gasped.

68
00:04:52.845 --> 00:04:56.608
"Messua! He looks like your boy!

69
00:04:57.324 --> 00:04:59.245
The one who was stolen by the tiger!"

70
00:05:00.826 --> 00:05:04.967
A woman with copper rings on her wrists and ankles stepped forward.

71
00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:07.769
She looked closely at Mowgli.

72
00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:12.891
"I'm not sure if he's my boy," she said at last.

73
00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:15.812
"But he does look like my son."

74
00:05:16.913 --> 00:05:18.733
The priest threw up his arms.

75
00:05:18.753 --> 00:05:24.576
"What the jungle has taken, the jungle has returned!

76
00:05:25.664 --> 00:05:27.187
Take the child home,
